# Mongoose Models

## Standard pattern

```typescript
import mongoose, { Schema, type Model } from "mongoose";
import type { ISomething } from "@/types";

const SomethingSchema = new Schema<ISomething>(
  {
    name: { type: String, required: true },
    userId: { type: Schema.Types.ObjectId, ref: "User", required: true },
  },
  { timestamps: true }
);

SomethingSchema.index({ userId: 1 });

const Something: Model<ISomething> =
  mongoose.models.Something || mongoose.model<ISomething>("Something", SomethingSchema);

export default Something;
```

## Rules

- Always use `{ timestamps: true }`.
- Type schemas with interfaces from `@/types/index.ts` (prefix with `I`).
- Use the hot-reload guard: `mongoose.models.X || mongoose.model(...)`.
- Default-export the model.
- Add indexes on the schema, not via `ensureIndex` at runtime.
- Connection is handled by `connectDB()` from `@/lib/db.ts` — repositories call it, not models.
